.TH DIFFVIM-PRECOMPUTED 1 "2026-08-16" "diffvim 1.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
diffvim-precomputed \- run diffvim with a diff computed by an external native tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B diffvim-precomputed
.RI [ options ]
.RI <oldfile>
.RI <newfile>
.br
.B diffvim-precomputed
.B \-h | \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B diffvim-precomputed
is a convenience wrapper that computes the diff between
.I oldfile
and
.I newfile
using one of the native compute tools (C, C++, Rust, or Go), then
launches
.B diffvim
with
.B \-\-precomputed
so the in-vim LCS computation is skipped.

This is 10-100x faster than the in-vim LCS for large files where the
vimscript LCS would take seconds or more. The compute tool runs in a
separate process and writes the precomputed diff to a temporary file,
which
.B diffvim
then reads.

.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I oldfile
Old version of the file to animate.
.TP
.I newfile
New version of the file to animate.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-tool c|cpp|rust|go
Which native compute tool to use (default:
.BR c ,
or
.BR $DIFFVIM_COMPUTE_TOOL ).
.TP
.B \-\-keep
Keep the precomputed diff file on exit (default: delete it).
.TP
.B \-\-time
Print compute + diffvim timing to stderr.
.TP
.B \-\-diffvim PATH
Override the
.B diffvim
binary to invoke (default:
.IR <script_dir>/diffvim ,
or
.BR $DIFFVIM_BIN ).
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help and exit.

.SH PASSTHROUGH OPTIONS
Any other option is forwarded verbatim to
.BR diffvim .
Common ones:
.RS
.IP \(bu 3
\fB\-\-algorithm\fR lcs|myers|patience
.IP \(bu 3
\fB\-\-semantic-cleanup\fR, \fB\-\-word-diff\fR, \fB\-\-indent-aware\fR
.IP \(bu 3
\fB\-\-optimize-sequence\fR, \fB\-\-no-optimize-sequence\fR, \fB\-\-left-to-right\fR
.IP \(bu 3
\fB\-\-preset\fR NAME
.IP \(bu 3
\fB\-\-speed\fR N, \fB\-\-output\fR FILE, \fB\-\-scroll\fR zz|zt|zb|none
.IP \(bu 3
\fB\-\-highlight-inline\fR, \fB\-\-highlight-hunk\fR, \fB\-\-dim-unchanged\fR
.RE
.PP
See
.BR diffvim (1)
for the full option list.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_COMPUTE_TOOL
Default
.B \-\-tool
value (c, cpp, rust, go).
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_COMPUTE_DIR
Directory containing
.I compute/bin/
(default: auto-detected from the script's location).
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_BIN
Override the
.B diffvim
binary (same as
.BR \-\-diffvim ).

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B diffvim-precomputed old.py new.py
Use the default C compute tool.
.TP
.B diffvim-precomputed --tool rust --time --semantic-cleanup old.py new.py
Use the Rust tool, print timing, enable semantic cleanup.
.TP
.B diffvim-precomputed --preset review --highlight-inline a.py b.py
Apply the \fBreview\fR preset and inline highlighting.
.TP
.B diffvim-precomputed --keep --time big_old.py big_new.py
Keep the precomputed file for inspection, print timing.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR diffvim (1),
.BR diffvim-compute (1),
.BR diffvim-compare (1)
.br
.I docs/PARALLEL_COMPUTE.md
covers the architecture and timing of the compute tools.
